.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt NL 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm nl
.Nd number input lines with logical page rules
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b Ar style
.Op Fl v Ar start
.Op Fl i Ar increment
.Op Fl w Ar width
.Op Fl s Ar separator
.Op Fl n Ar format
.Op Fl p
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Copy files to standard output with line numbers.
No files, or a file named
.Ql - ,
select standard input.
By default number nonempty body lines starting at 1, incrementing by 1,
right-aligned in a six-column field followed by a tab.
Empty lines are printed without a number.
.Pp
.Fl b Ar style
selects body numbering: a for every line, t for nonempty lines, n for none,
or p followed by a regular expression for matching lines.
.Fl v Ar start ,
.Fl i Ar increment ,
.Fl w Ar width
and
.Fl s Ar separator
change number start, increment, minimum width and following text.
.Fl n Ar format
selects ln, rn or rz for left, right, or zero-padded right alignment.
.Pp
Logical page delimiter lines can switch header, body and footer sections;
the default delimiter pair is backslash-colon, repeated three, two or one
times respectively.
Delimiters become blank output lines.
Numbering normally restarts on each logical page;
.Fl p
suppresses restarting.
Input files are only read; numbering does not edit them.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on successful processing; nonzero for bad options, invalid styles
or input/output failure. Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nl /etc/words.txt
.Ed
.Sh ABSD PROFILE
This is the unmodified uutils 0.12.0 utility pinned by the platform build.
The reference describes selected source-supported options; use
.Fl Fl help
for the complete upstream interface.
File access uses the process's ABSD filesystem view, output uses its
inherited stream, and the command acquires no additional authority.
There are no native Unix processes, signals or permission bits underneath
this port.
The command matrix exercises the example forms below; other options
listed here are source-checked, not separately guest-qualified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr head 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
